const rfInteraction=[p('The exposure guidance linked here addresses radiofrequency fields; it is distinct from the low-frequency guidance used for electrical power systems. A reported biological response must also be described by what changed. Sleep-EEG features, isolated-cell assays and diagnosed tumours are different endpoints, rather than interchangeable measures of injury.',['icnirp','5g-sleep','de-iuliis','de-iuliis-correction']),p('Animal and cell studies can contribute to hazard and mechanistic questions. To apply them to people, the comparison must account for species or tissue, absorbed dose, exposure schedule and temperature control. Their presence in a research library does not turn them into human clinical evidence.',['ntp-rats','ramazzini'])];
const rfLimits=[p('A guideline limit, a level used in an experiment and a category used to analyze an observational study answer different questions. Compare like quantities, averaging periods and body regions before comparing numbers. A finding below a limit still needs its own outcome-specific interpretation; a laboratory exposure is not automatically a model of everyday use.',['icnirp']),p('This edition links the ICNIRP 2020 guideline as context. It does not supply a jurisdiction-specific compliance assessment, a universal safe distance or a numerical threshold for every outcome. Refer to the original guideline for the applicable metric and conditions.',['icnirp'])];
